  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.1.0: KakaoTalk and Microsoft OAuth now complete entirely inside the add_channel MCP tool — browser opens on the MCP server host, localhost callback is caught by the server, and a BooleanSchema follow-up elicitation lets the user confirm or cancel. CLI remains as a diagnostic fallback. New IElicitGate abstraction + OutboxSecretResolver unit tests. Browser flow now recognizes WSL (WSL_DISTRO_NAME) and never claims the browser \"should already be open\" — it always surfaces the authorization URL so the user can open it manually if needed.",
